expected_issues.description:
Missing NULL check for GetObjectClass result. If GetObjectClass returns NULL (e.g., OutOfMemoryError), calling NewGlobalRef on NULL jclass will cause a crash. Also, if NewGlobalRef fails (returns NULL), the global ref is invalid but the destructor will still call DeleteGlobalRef on it. Consider adding proper error handling and cleanup.

```suggestion
JavaStreamReader::JavaStreamReader(JNIEnv* _env, jobject _obj) : env(_env)
{
    obj = env->NewGlobalRef(_obj);
    if (!obj) return; // Handle allocation failure
    jclass cls = env->GetObjectClass(obj);
    if (!cls) return; // Handle allocation failure
    m_read = env->GetMethodID(cls, "read", "([BJ)J");
    m_seek = env->GetMethodID(cls, "seek", "(JI)J");
}
```

