expected_issues.description:
**Missing JNI exception check**: After calling `NewByteArray`, you should check for JNI exceptions. If memory allocation fails, this could throw an OutOfMemoryError that needs to be handled.

**Suggested fix**:
```cpp
jbyteArray jBuffer = env->NewByteArray(static_cast<jsize>(size));
if (!jBuffer || env->ExceptionCheck()) {
    if (env->ExceptionCheck()) env->ExceptionClear();
    return 0;
}
```

