known_false_positives.description:
The member functions `read` and `seek` do not modify any member variables, so they should be marked as `const` to properly express their const-correctness and allow them to be called on const instances of the class.

```suggestion
    long long read(char* buffer, long long size) const CV_OVERRIDE;
    long long seek(long long offset, int way) const CV_OVERRIDE;
```
